## 1. Layered request flow

Every HTTP request flows through the same layers. CRUD lives in the domain service;
business processes live in their own application use-case. The domain never touches
the ORM directly — it depends on a repository **port**, with a TypeORM adapter behind it.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  HTTP[HTTP request] --> C[Controller]
  C -->|CRUD| S[Domain Service]
  C -->|business process| U[UseCase.execute]
  S --> P[Repository Port]
  U --> P
  P --> A[TypeORM Adapter]
  A --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
{{#if enableOutbox}}
  U -->|append in same tx| OB[(Outbox table)]
  OB --> R[Relay @Interval / SKIP LOCKED]
  R --> Q[[BullMQ queue]]
  Q --> W[Outbox Processor]
{{/if}}
```

